ployment to Claude autonomously. --- Current state The most recent sprint (Sprint A) executed a deep visual overhaul of Finance tabs T1â€“T3 (Executive Summary, Structure &amp; Concentration, Performance &amp; Attribution) using a combined Horizon UI Pro + Liquid Glass UI Playbook approach. Changes included: Deepened glassLight shadows (0.28 opacity), KPI tile textShadow glow, thicker 3.5px accent bars, boosted chart gradient fills (0.42â€“0.50), stronger hover lift (âˆ’4px / 1.006 scale), strengthened chartGlow filter (4.5px blur) T1: severity-coded alert pills, stronger radar (3px strokes), dual-area NW trajectory with drawdown overlay, decomposition bars with glow, Horizon-style Strengths/Weaknesses/Actions cards T2/T3: 0.90 fill opacity bars, stronger chart lines with drop-shadow glow, consistent 16px grid gaps A second commit added asset class donuts, debt summary panels, concentration composition bars, and beta/alpha/correlation KPIs with drawdown recovery analysis A comprehensive showcase document (LifeStackOSModuleShowcase.docx) was produced covering all 39 tabs with cover page, TOC, architecture overview, and per-tab detail (subtitle, KPI strip, panels, chart types, data sources). Active constraints: Bracket baseline: Braces 0 / Parens 7 / Brackets 0 No Treemap components; no localStorage JSX angle brackets must be wrapped as {"&gt;"} Unicode characters must use escape sequences in Python scripts (\u00A3, \u2192, \u2014) T14 appears before T13 in the file intentionally Glass is structure-first, effect-second â€” never heavy/cinematic on dense data surfaces; dense screens use quiet glass with readable inner plates --- On the horizon Remaining Finance tabs (T4â€“T15) visual overhaul to match Sprint A quality 122-item analytical additions roadmap across all tabs (Monte Carlo fan charts, decision attribution waterfalls, risk budget utilisation bars, probability-weighted milestone tracking, tax calendar countdowns, wrapper efficiency scoring, cycle position indicators, action priority scoring, etc.) Live data pipeline: Kubera + Monzo exports â†’ Supabase â†’ dashboard auto-recalc (ongoing refinement) Workflow automation architecture (37 workflows) to make both modules live and AI-powered â€” Phase 1 requires four API keys (FRED, Finnhub, CoinGecko, Kubera) Future LifeStack OS modules beyond Finance and Markets (Health, Social Graph, Growth Engine, etc.) --- Key learnings &amp; principles Density is a core design principle. The target aesthetic is a private family office CIO terminal â€” analytical depth and institutional credibility over decoration. Glass opacity must stay low on data-dense surfaces. Initial implementations set plate opacity too high (0.58â€“0.82), making tiles opaque. Correct values: Finance plates at 0.14 (T2), blur 26px, saturate 1.6â€“1.7. strreplace fails on JSX blocks longer than ~150 lines. The reliable pattern is a Python splice script: read full file, apply string replacements first, then split into lines and replace tab function blocks from highest line numbers downward (T3 â†’ T2 â†’ T1) to avoid line number shifts. Vercel SHA verification is the reliable deployment confirmation method. Match the returned SHA from listdeployments against git log --oneline rather than relying on push command output. When git push returns "Everything up-to-date," check git ls-remote origin main before re-pushing. api.github.com is blocked by the network proxy. All GitHub REST API calls fail. Working pattern: ask Alex to create repos via browser; push using PAT embedded directly in the HTTPS remote URL. Supabase audit after every deployment. Standard query uses UNION ALL SELECT 'tablename', count(*) FROM tablename across all 14 tables to confirm data integrity. Build validation: npx next build 2&gt;&amp;1 | tail -15 reliably surfaces JSX syntax errors before pushing. Recovery from syntax errors: git checkout -- components/FileName.jsx is the fastest path back to the last clean commit. The P object definition must never be caught by font-string replacement regexes â€” the mono: key in the palette definition has been accidentally converted in past sessions. --- Approach &amp; patterns Deployment workflow (user instruction â€” must follow exactly): Clone github.com/bouteralex-blip/lifestack-finance, edit incrementally, validate syntax, update Supabase (ynvfzssakggmmldjkmes) if needed, commit as "LifeStack Deploy", ask Alex for a temporary GitHub PAT to push, push to main, Vercel auto-deploys (prj5xoXKPM5DDyiriUC8jgQG5eQTA18). Claude does everything autonomously â€” Alex only provides the token. Never suggest manual deployment. Post-deployment audit (mandatory): Verify GitHub commit SHA on remote Confirm Vercel deployment state is READY (wait ~30 seconds before checking) Supabase 14-table row count audit Code syntax balance check Tab function integrity check useData.js mapping completeness Bug sweep Communication style: Alex is direct and concise. He expects autonomous execution with minimal explanation, provides GitHub PATs on request, and expects Claude to handle the full clone-edit-validate-commit-push-verify cycle independently. He pushes back clearly when something is overengineered. He communicates issues via brief verbal descriptions and expects root-cause diagnosis and clean fixes, not patches. Design implementation order: Horizon UI Pro structural backbone first â†’ Liquid Glass treatment on tiles/cards/panels â†’ LifeStack chart grammar, density rules, accents, and metrics overlay. --- Tools &amp; resources Infrastructure: GitHub: bouteralex-blip/lifestack-finance (public, repo ID 1178503455) â€” PAT authentication via inline HTTPS URL; tokens are single-use, revoked immediately after push Vercel: Project prj5xoXKPM5DDyiriUC8jgQG5eQTA18, team teamyJOnKVnF38JmRAieqsQE3BAs, auto-deploy from main in ~25 seconds Supabase: Project ynvfzssakggmmldjkmes (eu-west-1), 15 tables, all RLS-enabled Key codebase files: components/PortfolioVOS.jsx â€” Finance module (~3,100+ lines, T1â€“T15) components/MarketsModule.jsx â€” Markets module (~700 lines, 24 tabs) components/AppShell.jsx â€” Module switcher lib/useData.js â€” Supabase data hook with hardcoded fallbacks Design sources of truth: Horizon UI Pro Next.js template, Liquid Glass UI Playbook, LifeStack OS Design System v1, snippetchapter4_7.css, Finance Module Master Metric Guide v2 Chart libraries: Recharts (primary), Apache ECharts (echarts@5.5.0 + echarts-for-react@3.0.2) for radar, heatmaps, and correlation matrices Component library: Card, K (KPI tile), Grid, FlexRow, Hd, Ins, Tbl, Gauge, chart wrappers; design tokens in locked P colour object; three-tier liquid glass system via glassLight() Data sources: Kubera (portfolio tracking), Monzo (cash/transactions), Supabase (operational engine), Google Sheets (historical archive/audit trail), NotebookLM Pro (research library) AI toolkit: Claude Pro, ChatGPT Plus, Gemini Pro, Copilot Pro Subscriptions: Financial Times (paid), NotebookLM Pro, Kubera</p><p class="font-small text-text-500 opacity-60 pt-0.5">Last updated 7 days ago</p></div></div><div class="h-[0.5px] w-full bg-border-300"></div><div class="w-full px-[1.375rem] py-4 flex flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-1"><div class="w-full flex flex-col gap-0.5"><div class="h-6 w-full flex flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4"><h3 class="text-text-300 font-base-bold">Instructions</h3><div class="flex flex-row items-center gap-2"><div class="w-fit" data-state="closed"><button class="inline-flex
